    "Description": "Copy of a letter from Tracey Cameron to Cy Farley from September 25, 1977. The letter expresses Cameron's interest in the carousel figures, but not the scenery panels, and includes a proposal for the process of restoring and repainting the figures. Cameron estimates that the restoration would take less than one year and would cost $400 per figure as a base price. Cameron also states her preference to work in Hartford, Connecticut. The final page is signed by Cameron. Three pages total, stapled in the top left corner. The back of the third page has some notes written in blue ink. ",
